  <uml:Model xmi:id="_MqWNkOPxEfGg8KH2-CF6mA" name="VxCPS">
    <packageImport xmi:type="uml:PackageImport" xmi:id="_MzMAgePxEfGg8KH2-CF6mA">
      <importedPackage xmi:type="uml:Model" href="pathmap://UML_LIBRARIES/UMLPrimitiveTypes.library.uml#_0"/>
    </packageImport>
    <packageImport xmi:type="uml:PackageImport" xmi:id="_Mzs94OPxEfGg8KH2-CF6mA">
      <importedPackage xmi:type="uml:Package" href="pathmap://SysML16_LIBRARIES/SysML-Standard-Library.uml#SysML.package_packagedElement_Libraries"/>
    </packageImport>
    <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Package" xmi:id="_UiM6oOPxEfGg8KH2-CF6mA" name="Requirements">
      <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_6ua2QORuEfGD2PzXPcaESg" annotatedElement="_AaHtQORNEfGD2PzXPcaESg">
        <body>price = 1.2(BOM + 1000) &lt; 5113.20 ⇔ BOM &lt; 3261 eur&#xD;
. Current BOM = 929 + 334 + 2·999 = 3261 eur</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_wrixMORwEfGjsdib3d454A" annotatedElement="_AcI78ORMEfGD2PzXPcaESg">
        <body>Reference makespan 270.96 s, inverted tops and normal bottoms&#xD;
</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_Mz14oORxEfGjsdib3d454A" annotatedElement="_BQApEORxEfGjsdib3d454A">
        <body>The turner is the only resource that can invert pieces&#xD;
</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_bvA3cORxEfGjsdib3d454A" annotatedElement="_XpkzcORuEfGD2PzXPcaESg">
        <body>Fixing a field error costs eur&#xD;
1,000,000&#xD;
</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_lgSkQORxEfGjsdib3d454A" annotatedElement="_AcI78ORMEfGD2PzXPcaESg">
        <body>Faster components reduce makespan but raise BOM (BR-01.1) and energy (PR-01).&#xD;
</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="_t2OeYOc4EfGMO7H8UnEinw" annotatedElement="_rhacMORQEfGD2PzXPcaESg">
        <body>Design hypothesis: fast belts. -> To be confirmed after POOSL analysis: Needs to be >=30.2s makespan reduction to offset the 378eur price, and energy &lt;=2.0Mj (PR-01)&#xD;
</body>
      </ownedComment>
